Make d2s.c and f2s.c usable as headers.

The vendor tree installs ryu/d2s.c and ryu/f2s.c as ryu/d2s_impl.h and
ryu/f2s_impl.h (tools/vendor/manifest.tsv maps the names). This patch:

- makes every #include "ryu/..." relative to the including file;
- gives the entry points d2s_buffered_n, d2s_buffered, d2s and the f2s
  equivalents static inline linkage, in ryu.h and in the definitions;
- routes every assert() through RYU_ASSERT, which defaults to assert and
  which zufast defines away, so that no consumer's shared object
  references __assert_fail.

Upstream: to be submitted to ulfjack/ryu.

